Z||000000||Dan010||10-07-2001||08:53 AM||||I have a 86gt, with the optional instr pod.<BR>When I turn the key on, what lights should<BR>light up?<BR>door ajar, works<BR>service engine, works<BR>hi beam, works<BR>turn signal indicators, works<P>on the pod, both the volts, and oil lights<BR>work. is there any other that should be?<BR>Is there a light that comes on for fuel,<BR>or over heating?<P>I fixed me oil pressure gauge problem and<BR>the service engine (code 32) yesterday, thanks to all of you!!!!!!!!!<BR>Oil sending unit and a vacuum hose to the<BR>EGR sencer unit, <BR>Thanks for all the help<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||10-07-2001||11:41 AM||||The overheat should come on during bulb check but the factory screwed up the wires and the gage pegs instead.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan010||10-07-2001||06:22 PM||||Thanks, I guess all is fine, next I need to check on the motor and trans mounts<BR>Dan<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||10-07-2001||07:25 PM||||Does anyone have a wiring workaround for that? It CAN'T be good for the mechanisms...<P>||||reg||5
Z||000004||Devotshka||10-07-2001||08:16 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A> <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Does anyone have a wiring workaround for that? It CAN'T be good for the mechanisms...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||3
Z||000005||ssalyers||10-07-2001||08:21 PM||||When I took the instrument cluster apart for cleaning, I got out my dremel tool and drilled a very small hole next to the temp gauge and inserted a cut nail (painted black) to stop the gauge.  Works great and look O.E.<P>--Shawn||||reg||12
Z||000006||Phil||10-07-2001||08:39 PM||||You can correct the factory error by reversing the wires at the sender and at the connector that plugs into the dash. This reversing puts the "bulb check" on the light and not the gage||||reg||1
